/-
Abs, by the Lean-native checker (LCheck/Check.lean), run by
`native_decide` on gocheck's input for the specification of gocheck/specs.sh
(Checkers/Native/Inputs.lean, generated by gocheck/native.sh).

`abs_triple` is `triple_holds` for that input, from `lcheck_sound`. The
input is gocheck's (untrusted) reading of the Go source, so
`abs_func_val` checks, by `rfl`, that the input's function is exactly
Goose's translation of `Abs`.

Trusted, beyond the Lean kernel: the compiler that `native_decide` evaluates
`lcheck` with, through the axiom it adds (`#print axioms` shows it as
`<theorem>._native.native_decide.ax_1_1`: the compiled code returned `true`).
`gocheck/native_bench.sh` also times the same check run by the kernel
(`decide +kernel`), which adds no axiom.
-/
import Checkers.Native.Sound
import Checkers.Native.Inputs

namespace Perennial
namespace Checker
namespace Native

open github_com.upamanyus.bootstrap_go

theorem abs_func_val [FfiSyntax] [GoGlobalContext] :
    func_val abs_func = checker.examples.Abs.impl := rfl

theorem abs_triple : triple_holds abs_func abs_vars abs_pre abs_post :=
  lcheck_sound _ _ _ _ (by native_decide)

end Native
end Checker
end Perennial
